WEBVTT

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:21.450
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.550
Don't go!

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.460
No!

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.060
Enchu!

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:27.530
Enchu!

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:33.710
Got Questions About Spirits? Ask Us!
We Offer Consultations for Those Troubled by Spirits
The Muhyo Bureau of Supernatural Investigation 
Advertisement by: Kusano Jiro 

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.720
<b>Muhyo Bureau of
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.870
<b>Muhyo Bureau of
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.490
Muhyo! Give it back!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.850
This is good stuff, Roji!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.680
I'm the one who bought it!

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:06.510
Jabin

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.780
You brute!

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.640
Hey...

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.340
<b>Article 1
Rie and Taeko</b>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.400
Jeez...

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.350
We almost lost a client.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.890
A-Anyway, let's start over.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.800
If you're having trouble with spirits,
leave it to us!

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.360
Welcome to our Muhyo Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation!

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.360
<b>Muhyo Bureau of
 Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.160
This is our Magical Law Executor, Muhyo Toru.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.370
Hmph. More work to do?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.370
<b>Magical Law Executor
Muhyo Toru</b>

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.620
And I'm his assistant, Kusano Jiro.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.620
<b>Assistant
Kusano Jiro</b>

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.310
<b>Roji</b>

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.310
<b>Muhyo</b>

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.330
You can call us Muhyo and Roji!

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.630
Don't leave! Don't leave!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.610
Idiot.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.380
So, um...

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.910
Could you tell us your name?

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.890
Inoue. Inoue Rie.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.540
What? Why so antisocial?

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.120
<b>Shh</b>

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.590
Shh!

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.050
What brings you here today, Rie-chan?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.210
Is magical law like... exorcisms and stuff?

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.860
Yeah, basically.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.220
The number of crimes caused by
evil spirits is rising by the year,

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.200
Death

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.200
Erasure

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.200
Murder

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.200
Threats

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.200
so we enforce various punishments for them!

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.200
<b>Magical Law</b>

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.150
Sounds like a scam.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.890
You think so?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.020
Would you like a demonstration?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.960
I'd rather not bother, but I will.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.660
Move the table.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.950
Sure.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.190
Your legs have felt heavy lately, right?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.390
Huh?

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.360
Animal spirits!

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:04.810
According to Magical Law Article 884,

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:08.140
<b>Crime:
Unsolicited Animal Spirit Parasitism</b>

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.400
for the crime of "Unsolicited 
Animal Spirit Parasitism,"

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.720
I sentence you to "Death by Exorcism"!

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:09.780
<b>Sentence: Death by Exorcism</b>

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.220
That's what magical law is.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:31.990
So I take it you want me to send
some ghost to the afterlife or Hell?

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.160
T-Track 5...

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.740
Rie-chan should be out 
of school for the day...

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.880
Hey. What's the meaning of this?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.840
Well, obviously, we're disguised as 
detectives so Rie-chan won't recognize—

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.070
This just makes us more conspicuous!

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.590
I guess people do have hidden sides...

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.710
but Rie-chan looks more 
cheerful than I expected.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:14.840
Huh?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.340
She moved to another table?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.850
She doesn't look well at all!

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.570
What's going on?

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.440
She saw the platform, I bet.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.200
It was in plain sight from that other table...

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.460
Track 5 of the train station.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.710
Th-The girl of track 5?

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.690
Yeah.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:51.060
There's a rumor that a girl's ghost appears
at the track 5 platform of Hashiki Station.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.970
I know about that.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:56.960
Huh?!

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.850
So, what about her?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.250
The rumors say that the girl of track 5

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.900
is a classmate of mine, Okazaki Taeko.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.320
She was my friend.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.250
I think she's having trouble moving on.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:17.700
Because Taeko was...

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.090
I was basically the one who killed her.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.470
Hey, Rie! Let's hold hands!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.650
We were really close.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.310
After we started high school, 
neither of us fit in very well,

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.070
and then our eyes met...

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.770
Wish they'd shut up.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:42.100
Yeah.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.610
We planned ahead every day
so our hairstyles would match.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.230
Rie, the braided version!

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.210
Oh, come on...

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.380
We were always together.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.410
And here, you do this.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.330
Oh...

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.690
We didn't care what other people thought.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.010
They're so gross.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.900
Aren't they a little <i>too</i> close?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.640
Ew, they're looking this way!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.340
Cut it out, seriously!

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.620
Hey...

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.130
No matter what happens to us...

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.810
even when we get old...

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.510
It's okay.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:37.070
If anything ever happens, I'll protect you.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:41.640
Okay!

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.330
It's a promise!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.170
Then, one day, Taeko was absent with a cold.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:51.710
<b>Taeko</b>

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.240
Sure. Take care.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.910
Get plenty of rest.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:01.310
Some girls on the volleyball team,
who'd apparently taken notice of my height,

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.900
came and talked to me.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:07.600
Suddenly, my world changed.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.240
That was awesome!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.120
You rock, Rie-chan!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.180
Nice course!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:20.440
That was crazy!

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:27.240
For a few days, everything I saw
seemed to be shining.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.420
Why didn't you come visit me?

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.270
S-Sorry!

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.190
I was so lonely!

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.240
Hey, Rie!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.140
Can you fill in again? We're one short!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.370
It's just a practice match, but...

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.520
Sorry, Taeko.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.940
I'll probably be late, 
so go home without me.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.190
Wait! What about... tomorrow's hairstyle...

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.690
That kind of thing went on for a few days.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:09:59.850
Rie...

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:01.830
Rie...

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.790
Rie-chan, you're seriously amazing!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.890
You should join the team officially.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.250
But...

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.910
Yeah, you should!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:13.780
Rie...

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.220
Why?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:21.470
You changed... your hair... 
without telling me?

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.720
Taeko, there's a reason for this...

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.200
We made a promise!

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:28.950
Whoa!

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:29.480
What?!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.670
Why are you so distant lately?

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.880
Why don't you leave school with me?

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.640
Who are these people?!

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:41.010
Please! Don't take my Rie from me!

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.520
Please!

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.740
Not my Rie!

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.580
I thought of her as a nuisance.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:54.050
A new world had finally 
opened itself to me...

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:58.600
I had finally made some new friends...

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.650
Rie...

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:03.850
Hold...

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.180
No way!

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.610
Hold...

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.740
my hand...

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:29.000
<b>The Devil's Shadow</b>

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.000
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:35.000
<b>Beelzebub's Treasure Chest</b>

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.000
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.500
Uh, Muhyo...

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:41.410
Did you really tell Rie-chan to come 
to track 5 this late at night?

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.760
It'll be better to have her draw out Taeko.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.750
Or would <i>you</i> rather go?

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.470
Huh?! N-No, that's not what I meant!

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:55.760
Okay, here's the plan.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.290
We'll follow you in later
so the ghost won't suspect anything.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:00.990
You can go on to track 5—

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.160
Rie-chan?!

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:09.110
What's wrong? If you want out,
you'd better say so now.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.920
<i>Taeko...</i>

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.130
Will she be okay?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.180
Who cares?

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:28.100
But if her friend became 
a ghost because of her...

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.270
<i>Roji-san?</i>

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.640
<i>I can't see through the fog...</i>

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.870
<i>I-I have to go.</i>

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.030
Hey, you two!

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:44.170
What are you doing here at this hour?

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.280
Tch!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:50.540
I declare Special Magical Law, Clause 11...

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.410
<b>Special Magical Law</b>

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.410
<b>Clause 11</b>

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.220
<b>Anesthetic Needles</b>

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.450
Anesthetic Needles!

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:06.550
You're not supposed to use 
magical law on civilians.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.270
They'll just be asleep for 
three days and nights.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.470
Jeez, come on...

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.230
<i>This is it.</i>

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.720
<i>This is where Taeko...</i>

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:30.050
<i>N-No... I just...</i>

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:31.700
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:32.740
Rie...

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.710
Are you really...

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.610
really...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.700
really, really, really...

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.210
Rie?

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.140
Hold...

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.380
my hand!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.360
Muhyo, is that...

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.610
It's Taeko's spirit.

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:08.520
It's not so much a ghost as a monster.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:13.300
In ectoplasm this thick,
there must be a lot of bound spirits.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.760
<b>Ectoplasm</b>

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.500
And their grudges must've resonated
with hers, leading to this.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:24.020
You won't hold my hand?

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:28.970
No... Taeko...

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.210
Hold my hand!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.860
Rie-chan!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.270
Tch!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.520
Oh, no! It's swallowing her up!

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.780
Quit screeching!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.980
According to Magical Law Article 244,

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.420
"Unsolicited Object—"

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.160
Muhyo, look out!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:10.250
I won't let anyone get between me and Rie!

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:13.650
Look... Look!

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:22.730
I can hold this many hands with Rie!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.110
Taeko...

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.940
Good for you.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.820
Those'll be useful in Hell!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.330
For the crimes of 
"Unsolicited Object Spectralization"

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.730
<b>Crimes: Unsolicited Object Spectralization</b>

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.450
and "Obstruction of Magical Law"...

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.730
<b>and Obstruction of Magical Law</b>

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:48.550
I sentence you to "Hades's Banquet"!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.380
<b>Sentence: Hades's Banquet</b>

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.940
<b>Hades's Banquet</b>

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.910
Wh-Why'd it take Rie-chan, too?!

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.110
Shut up and watch.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.790
When Hades doesn't like 
the taste of something...

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.210
Rie-chan! Are you okay?!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.970
Taeko...

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.270
Idiot.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:43.980
Huh?

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:46.490
She's much smaller now...

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:51.170
Hades's saliva must have 
reduced her spirit energy.

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:53.490
But...

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.250
What did he say?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:04.370
"Return my dinner, or you 
will all go to Hell."

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.120
Huh?!

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:10.000
Can't we at least make it so 
Taeko-chan doesn't go to Hell?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.210
Can't you do something, Muhyo?!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.220
You seem to be misunderstanding something.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:20.980
Taeko committed a crime.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.500
Crimes must be punished.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:31.980
Taeko!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:36.490
Hades's stomach is connected to Hell.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:41.120
You realize what'll happen
if you don't let go, don't you?

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.120
Taeko... I'm sorry.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:50.630
If I'd held on to your hand that day...

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:55.940
But I won't let go of you again!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.340
You're sure?

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.200
I'm sure!

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.170
I...

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:04.920
No.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.850
You can't, Rie.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.860
I'm happy...

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:25.090
I'm happy you held on...

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:48.580
Taeko!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.360
Hades changed his mind.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:15.710
Taeko's destination will 
be the River Styx instead.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:23.430
Oh, Muhyo...

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.580
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.250
This didn't involve me.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.780
Two Days Later

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:44.690
Hello!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:47.300
Not here today, either?

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:49.720
Okay.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.790
Rie-chan seems happy.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:58.050
I'm sad we won't see her again,

00:19:58.600 --> 00:19:59.840
but Muhyo makes the rules.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:03.780
And one of them is that we don't see
the client again once the job's done.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.280
Bye-bye.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.380
But...

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.340
Where do you think you're going?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.370
Can't I just talk a little bit 
with Rie-chan if I'm in disguise?

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.570
Your disguise is only gonna 
get you laughed at!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.130
Aw, why?!

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:30.160
You usually sleep for three days 
after using magical laws...

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.120
<b>Thank you so much.
Inoue Rie
Speaking for Taeko in Heaven</b>

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:39.000
<b>Thank you so much.
Inoue Rie
Speaking for Taeko in Heaven</b>

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:35.810
I'm really glad, though.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:39.000
Those two were saved by their friendship.

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:41.960
Friendship, nothing.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.730
Shut the curtain. I'm going to sleep.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:47.760
Huh?!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:52.530
Oh, I guess you're still sleepy after all.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.000
Muhyo.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.540
Let's learn about magical law!

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.540
(with video)

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.540
<b>Kusano Jiro 
